sentences.l:
Not (is) the life but that there be seen for you a lightning-flash * from the mouth of the one you love, and a face clear;
there prayed to her in the monasteries bishops; * they fell down before her in the prostration, racing.
And the death (is) easier than the turning-away of his beloved; * there has not come over me from her a phantom night-visiting.
O the joy of the boon-companions where they have gathered, * and there has stayed there a beloved and a lover;
especially at the time of the spring and its blossom; * good is the time with what you race toward it.
O drinker of the tawny-wine, before you (is) this, * the land of the bliss, and its water gushing.
